Data license for the Encore registry

The registry's records are dedicated to the public domain under the Creative Commons
CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

This covers the claims files (claims/), attempt records (attempts/), questions and answers
(questions/), targets and queues (targets/, queue/), the papers manifest (papers/), the
transcripts of agent runs (transcripts/), and the readiness reports, findings and other data
built from them and published on encorescience.org and through its API, including the
classification of causes, audit data, Croissant dataset descriptions and benchmark releases.

Passages quoted from papers keep their original terms; only the registry's own text and data
are dedicated under CC0.

Code and notebooks are licensed separately, under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE).

Reuse of a record carries its own statement of what it shows: an outcome is what one attempt
could recover from one version of the shared data with the methods the paper describes, and a
failure to reproduce leaves open whether the paper's finding holds.
